.Dd April 22, 2026
.Dt CC 1
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm cc
.Nd Substrate C compiler driver
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op options
.Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
compiles C sources, runs the preprocessor, emits assembly/object output, and
links via
.Xr as 1
and
.Xr ld 1 .
.Pp
When invoked as
.Nm cpp ,
preprocessor-only mode is selected.
.Pp
.Dv __BITINT_MAXWIDTH__
is 65535:
.Vt _BitInt Ns Pq Ar N
of any width up to it, and
.Li wb
and
.Li uwb
constants of any size, are laid out and passed as gcc does, with
multiplication, division and the floating conversions done by
libgcc's
.Fn __mulbitint3 ,
.Fn __divmodbitint4 ,
.Fn __floatbitint*
and
.Fn __fix*bitint ,
but for a product of two 64-bit limbs on x86-64
.Po
.Vt __int128 ,
.Vt _BitInt Ns Pq 65
to
.Vt _BitInt Ns Pq 128
.Pc ,
made inline with
.Li mulq ,
as gcc makes it.
.Vt __int128
and
.Vt unsigned __int128
exist on x86-64, where
.Dv __SIZEOF_INT128__
is 16; on i386 they are rejected and
.Dv __SIZEOF_INT128__
is left undefined, as gcc does.
.Pp
gcc's x86 named address spaces,
.Li __seg_fs
and
.Li __seg_gs ,
are type qualifiers: an object in one, through a pointer to one, a member
of one or declared in one, is read and written through
.Li %fs
or
.Li %gs ,
the address its offset there, and an inline asm memory operand of one is
printed with the segment, as Linux's per-CPU data needs.
Copying a structure into one is refused.
.Pp
.Li #pragma pack Ns Pq Ar n ,
.Li pack() ,
.Li pack(push Ns Op , Ar n Ns )
and
.Li pack(pop) ,
and the same through
.Li _Pragma ,
hold the members of the structures declared after them to alignment
.Ar n ,
as gcc does: one an
.Sq Li aligned
attribute asks more of and a bit-field's storage unit too, while a
structure's own
.Sq Li aligned
still counts.
.Pp
gcc's
.Sq Li counted_by Ns Pq Ar m
on a flexible array member or a pointer member names the member holding
its count, and
.Fn __builtin_counted_by_ref p->fam
is the address of that member, or a null
.Vt void *
where the member has none, as gcc gives it; no bounds are checked by it.
.Pp
Vector types, GNU
.Sq Li vector_size
and clang's
.Sq Li ext_vector_type ,
are laid out, operated on element by element, and passed and returned
as gcc (and clang) do: on i386 a 16-byte vector travels in
.Li %xmm0
to
.Li %xmm2
and an 8-byte one in an MMX register, so code that calls gcc-built
functions taking 8-byte vectors must not rely on the x87 until the
caller has issued
.Li emms ,
as
.Nm
does.
.Pp
.Vt _Decimal32 ,
.Vt _Decimal64
and
.Vt _Decimal128
hold the BID encoding gcc uses, and their arithmetic and conversions
call libgcc's
.Fn __bid_*
functions, so a program using them links only against a libgcc built
with decimal floating point (a Linux host's is; substrate's is not).
.Pp
Installed host-runnable copies of
.Nm ,
.Xr as 1 ,
and
.Xr ld 1
are typically staged with
.Dq Li make host_dist
and installed with
.Dq Li sudo make HOST_DIST_PREFIX=/opt/substrate host_install .
See
.Xr host_toolchain 7
for the full install and
.Ev PATH
workflow.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "-pedantic-errors"
.It Fl E
Preprocess only.
.It Fl S
Compile to assembly.
.It Fl c
Compile and/or assemble only, do not link.
.It Fl o Ar file
Set output path.
With
.Fl E
or
.Fl S ,
a
.Ar file
of
.Ql -
is standard output; with
.Fl c
or when linking it is a file named
.Ql - ,
as with
.Xr gcc 1 .
.It Fl I Ar dir , Fl D Ar name Ns Op =value , Fl U Ar name
Preprocessor include/macro controls.
A
.Fl D
that gives a macro already defined, by the compiler or an earlier
.Fl D ,
another value is warned of, as gcc does, and is an error under
.Fl Werror .
.It Fl idirafter Ar dir
Add a late include search path.
.It Fl include Ar file , Fl imacros Ar file
Forced include/macro inputs.
.It Fl P
Suppress line markers in preprocessor output.
.It Fl trigraphs
Replace trigraphs
.Pq Ql ??=
for
.Ql #
and so on.
As with
.Xr gcc 1 ,
they are replaced by default only in the ISO modes before C23
.Pq Fl std Ns = Ns Ar c99 , not Ar gnu99 .
.It Fl dM
Dump macro definitions.
.It Fl M , Fl MM , Fl MD , Fl MMD
Emit dependency rules.
.It Fl MF Ar file , Fl MT Ar target , Fl MQ Ar target
Dependency output target controls.
.It Fl std Ns = Ns Ar c90|c95|c99|c11|c17|c23
Language mode.
.Dv __STDC_VERSION__
is not defined in C90 (as the standard has it), and is 199409L for
.Ar iso9899:199409 .
.It Fl ansi
The same as
.Fl std Ns = Ns Ar c89 .
.It Fl O0 , Fl O1 , Fl O2 , Fl O3 , Fl O , Fl Os , Fl Oz , Fl Og , Fl Ofast
Optimization level.
.Fl O
alone is
.Fl O1 ,
as in
.Xr gcc 1 ,
and so are its named levels:
.Fl Os
and
.Fl Oz
are
.Fl O2 ,
.Fl Og
is
.Fl O1
and
.Fl Ofast
is
.Fl O3 .
Every level above 0 currently runs the same passes.
From
.Fl O1
a call of a small
.Ic static inline
(or
.Ic always_inline )
function of the same file is replaced by the function's body, and what
that makes constant is folded, so a call a constant helper guards is
dropped with its dead branch, as with
.Xr gcc 1 .
So is a call of a
.Ic static
function called from that one place only and named nowhere else (its
address not taken, not
.Ic used ,
.Ic weak
or
.Ic noinline ) ,
whatever its size within reason, and the function is then not emitted,
unless it is on a cycle of calls or its locals would make the caller's
frame larger than 256 bytes and either larger than 1024 bytes or more
than eleven times what it was,
as with
.Xr gcc 1 Ns 's
.Fl finline-functions-called-once .
A local variable whose address is not taken, and that is read and
written whole, is kept as a value rather than in memory; a copy is read
as what it copies; and arithmetic that leaves its operand as it was
(a mask of all ones, adding zero, a truth value compared unequal to
zero) is dropped.
A parameter of a
.Ic static
function that every call of it passes the same constant, its address
not taken, is that constant within it, as with
.Xr gcc 1 Ns 's
interprocedural constant propagation.
At
.Fl O0
nothing is inlined.
.Pp
At every level the i386 code generator keeps values in registers from
one instruction to the next within a block, writes back only what is
read again, uses a constant operand as an immediate, and branches on a
compare's flags when the branch is all that reads it.
.It Fl m32 , Fl m64
Target i386 or x86_64 ABI.
The default is the ABI
.Nm
was itself built for: x86_64 on a 64-bit system, i386 on a 32-bit one.
The target's runtime is used: startup code from
.Pa /usr/lib
or
.Pa /usr/lib64 ,
the C library from
.Pa /lib
or
.Pa /lib64 ,
and
.Pa /sbin/ld.so
or
.Pa /sbin/ld64.so
as the program's interpreter.
A 64-bit program is linked as a position-independent executable; a
32-bit one is not, as the i386 code generator writes position-dependent
code.
.It Fl mpreferred-stack-boundary Ns = Ns Ar n
Keep the stack aligned to 2^n bytes at a call, n from 2 to 12, rather
than the psABI's 16; with 2 or 3 a function's frame is not padded for
it, nor a call's arguments.
On x86-64, where Linux builds with 3, the stack is then 8-byte aligned:
a function with an object of 16-byte alignment in its frame keeps a
frame pointer and aligns the stack pointer to 16 bytes itself, as gcc
does.
.It Fl msse , Fl mno-sse
On i386, whether SSE instructions may be used.
On x86-64,
.Fl mno-sse
leaves the vector registers alone where nothing uses them: a variadic
function does not save them for
.Xr stdarg 3 ,
which it otherwise does only when its caller says in
.Li %al
that it passed any, as gcc does.
.It Fl mcmodel Ns = Ns Cm small | kernel | medium | large
x86-64: where the code and its data are linked.
With
.Cm kernel ,
a global declared
.Sy extern
is reached relative to
.Li %rip
as any other is, not through the GOT, which a kernel has none of; the
others change nothing.
.It Fl g
Emit debug information.
.It Fl fasynchronous-unwind-tables , Fl funwind-tables
.It Fl fno-asynchronous-unwind-tables , Fl fno-unwind-tables
Whether the frame descriptions
.Fl g
emits go to
.Li .eh_frame ,
loaded with the code, as by default, or only to
.Li .debug_frame ,
for a debugger.
.It Fl fjump-tables , Fl fno-jump-tables
Whether a
.Ic switch
of enough cases, dense enough, is a jump through a table, as by default,
or always a chain of compares.
Linux builds code that runs before it is relocated with
.Fl fno-jump-tables :
a table's absolute entries would send it nowhere.
The last of the two given counts.
.It Fl fomit-frame-pointer , Fl fno-omit-frame-pointer
Whether a function addresses its frame off the stack pointer and has
.Li %ebp
.Pq Li %rbp
to allocate, as Linux builds with, where that makes it smaller, or keeps a
frame pointer, as by default.
A function that takes its frame's address, moves the stack pointer itself
.Pq Fn alloca , a variable-length array ,
takes variadic arguments, or has an inline asm whose operand is a memory slot
or an asm goto keeps one, and so does every function under
.Fl g .
.It Fl Wall , Fl Werror
Warning controls.
.It Fl pedantic , Fl pedantic-errors
Standards conformance diagnostics.
.It Fl fPIC
Generate position-independent code.
On i386 a symbol that binds within the object (a static one, a label,
or one of hidden, protected or internal visibility) is addressed from
the GOT's address, found with a pc thunk, at
.Li sym@GOTOFF ;
another through its GOT entry,
.Li sym@GOT ;
and a call of one goes through
.Li sym@PLT
with the GOT in
.Li %ebx ,
which every function then saves and restores.
The code holds no absolute relocation.
On x86-64 such a symbol is reached relative to
.Li %rip
and only another through its GOT entry,
.Li sym@GOTPCREL ;
with
.Fl fPIE
a global defined in the file binds within it too.
.It Fl fgnu89-inline , Fl fno-gnu89-inline
Use, or do not use, GNU89 inline semantics, the reverse of C99's: a
plain
.Ic inline
function definition is an external definition, and an
.Ic extern inline
one is for inlining only and defines no external symbol.
.Nm
emits an inline-only definition as a local copy, which
.Fl O1
and up inline where they can, as any
.Ic static inline
function.
.It Fl ftrivial-auto-var-init Ns = Ns Cm zero|pattern|uninitialized
With
.Cm zero ,
an automatic variable declared without an initializer starts as zero:
a structure, union or array has every byte cleared, as a scalar always
has.  A variable-length array is not cleared.
.Cm pattern
gives such an aggregate gcc's pattern instead, every byte 0xfe.
.Cm uninitialized ,
the default, leaves an aggregate as the stack had it.
.It Fl fsanitize Ns = Ns Ar list , Fl -param Ar name Ns = Ns Ar value
Taken, as gcc takes them, and acted on no more than the other gcc options
.Nm
ignores: no code is instrumented, and a note says so for each
.Fl fsanitize
taken (a note, which
.Fl Werror
does not make an error, as a build's probes for the option need it taken).
A sanitizer gcc does not have
.Pq Cm kernel-memory , Cm kcfi
is refused, as are clang's
.Fl falloc-token-max ,
.Fl fsanitize-coverage-stack-depth-callback-min ,
.Fl frandomize-layout-seed-file ,
.Fl fsanitize-cfi-* ,
.Fl fms-anonymous-structs
and
.Fl mllvm ,
so that a build probing for them finds them missing.
.It Fl shared
Link shared object.
.It Fl pthread
Enable pthread compile/link behavior.
.It Fl emit-ssa
Validate input textual IR via
.Xr ir-verifier 1 .
.It Fl fdump-ir Ns Op = Ns Cm all
Write the intermediate representation the back end is given, in the
text form
.Xr ir-verifier 1
reads, to
.Ar name Ns Pa .ir ,
where
.Ar name
is the output file without its suffix when
.Fl o
names the assembly or object file, and otherwise the input's base
name in the current directory.
With
.Cm all ,
write it after each middle-end pass instead, to
.Ar name Ns Pa .lower.ir ,
.Ar name Ns Pa .legalize.ir
and
.Ar name Ns Pa .opt.ir .
.It Fl v
Verbose tool invocation.
.It Fl ###
Print pipeline commands without executing.
.It Fl -bootstrap-gcc
Temporary C-to-assembly fallback via host gcc.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width CC_MIR_LIMIT
.It Ev AS , LD
The assembler and linker to run, instead of the ones beside
.Nm .
.It Ev CC_NO_MIR
With the value 1, code is emitted with every value in a stack slot,
not through the register allocator.
.It Ev CC_MIR_LIMIT
A number
.Ar n :
only the first
.Ar n
functions the register allocator would take go through it, to
find a function it miscompiles by bisection.
.It Ev CC_MIR_STATS
With the value 1, print to the standard error each function the
register allocator takes, and why it does not take each other one.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
If a tool
.Nm
runs
.Pq Xr as 1 , Xr ld 1
cannot be executed, or is killed by a signal,
.Nm
says so and exits non-zero.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr as 1 ,
.Xr cpp 1 ,
.Xr ir-diff 1 ,
.Xr ir-normalize 1 ,
.Xr ir-verifier 1 ,
.Xr ld 1 ,
.Xr host_toolchain 7
